The root cause of the syntax error at line 104 is the use of curly braces to define the body of the function requestClassification. In Alloy 6, curly braces are reserved for predicates and facts, while functions must use the '=' syntax with a single expression as the body. The parser encounters an unexpected semicolon after the closing brace because it is not expecting a block statement for a function definition. Previous attempts focused on the presence or absence of a semicolon or on the internal expression; however, the primary violation is the use of curly braces for a function body rather than the required '=' syntax.

