[RATIONALE]:
This fix directly aligns with Alloy 6's function declaration rules and is fundamentally different from prior attempts, which retained curly braces or only addressed trailing semicolons. Using '=' removes the block structure and enforces the required single-expression function body.

[LESSON]:
In Alloy 6, always define functions using '=' and a single expression, never with curly braces or block syntax—this prevents top-level parsing errors and enforces correct function semantics.
